{
  "schema_version": "prompt-runtime.program-scenario.v1",
  "story_path": "user_stories/test-suite-queue-ports.md",
  "criteria": [
    {
      "id": "AC1",
      "text": "`suiteQueueRoot` resolves `PDD_SUITE_QUEUE`, `PDD_VM_SUITE_LOCK.queue`, or `/tmp/pdd-full-suite-UID` from `process.current`, and throws `Error` when the resolved path is relative."
    },
    {
      "id": "AC2",
      "text": "`suiteStatusWords` formats waiting, running, finished, failed, and unavailable status lines and throws `Error` when `suite` is invalid."
    },
    {
      "id": "AC3",
      "text": "`calculateCheckCapacity`, `configureCheckCapacity`, `releaseCheckCapacity`, and `readCheckStatus` compute and persist `capacity.json` under `lock.acquire` and `lock.release`, count running and waiting tickets from `fs.readdir` and `files.read`, and throw `Error` on invalid observations or owners."
    },
    {
      "id": "AC4",
      "text": "`readSuiteProgress` returns the latest ticket progress and paused duration for `cwd`, returns `{state: \"unavailable\", reason, pausedMs: 0}` when queue records are unreadable, and throws `Error` when `cwd` is invalid."
    },
    {
      "id": "AC5",
      "text": "`executeSuite` and `runTestSuite` enforce command and timeout rules, allocate and clean up the isolated suite environment under the queue root, record ticket receipts and validation logs, and verify descendant process-group termination via `process.groupAlive`."
    }
  ],
